FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: josephine-the-singer.
FILED BY: the mouse folk, assembled, unsure why.

OFF THE RECORD: Kafka's last story, and the selective receive. The
OFF THE RECORD: folk commence two of their own: an ordinary mouse,
OFF THE RECORD: and Josephine, who sings, or at any rate squeaks in a
OFF THE RECORD: manner she regards as singing. Both reply; the folk
OFF THE RECORD: choose to hear Josephine FIRST, whatever order the
OFF THE RECORD: replies arrived in: AWAIT SUMMONS FROM consumes the
OFF THE RECORD: first notice bearing the named case's seal, out of
OFF THE RECORD: turn, and everything passed over keeps its place in
OFF THE RECORD: line for the plain AWAIT SUMMONS that follows. Then,
OFF THE RECORD: as the story requires, Josephine vanishes, and the
OFF THE RECORD: folk wait for her one last time, with a deadline,
OFF THE RECORD: because grief also must be scheduled.

HEREINAFTER, patience SHALL MEAN 2.

ARTICLE 1.
    OFF THE RECORD: One mouse is much like another; the same filing serves for both.
    COMMENCE PROCEEDINGS UPON "FORM K-1. IN THE MATTER OF: one-of-the-folk. ARTICLE 1. AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER home. AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER voice. SERVE NOTICE OF voice UPON home. ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.", FILED UNDER mouse.
    COMMENCE PROCEEDINGS UPON "FORM K-1. IN THE MATTER OF: one-of-the-folk. ARTICLE 1. AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER home. AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER voice. SERVE NOTICE OF voice UPON home. ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.", FILED UNDER josephine.

ARTICLE 2.
    SERVE NOTICE OF THE CASE AT BAR UPON mouse.
    SERVE NOTICE OF "an ordinary squeak" UPON mouse.
    SERVE NOTICE OF THE CASE AT BAR UPON josephine.
    SERVE NOTICE OF "piping, if not song" UPON josephine.

ARTICLE 3.
    OFF THE RECORD: The concert. Josephine is heard first, by name;
    OFF THE RECORD: the squeak, passed over, has lost nothing but its precedence.
    AWAIT SUMMONS FROM josephine, FILED UNDER song.
    PROCLAIM "first, whatever arrived first, Josephine: " PLUS song.
    AWAIT SUMMONS, FILED UNDER squeak.
    PROCLAIM "then the folk, in their turn: " PLUS squeak.

ARTICLE 4.
    OFF THE RECORD: Josephine vanishes, as she does. The folk await
    OFF THE RECORD: her voice once more, but the folk are practical.
    AWAIT SUMMONS FROM josephine FOR AT MOST patience DAYS, FILED UNDER encore. FAILING WHICH, REFER TO ARTICLE 5.
    PROCLAIM "an encore, against all precedent: " PLUS encore.
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.

ARTICLE 5.
    PROCLAIM "Josephine has vanished. The folk, who do not mourn, continue.".
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
